[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3514451023","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112617#issuecomment-3514451023","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112617","id":3514451023,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RekRP","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-11T00:20:21Z","updated_at":"2025-11-11T00:21:36Z","body":"> with the `em` suffix\r\n\r\nI'm curious if we should go with [`rem`](https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/css/difference-between-em-and-rem-units-in-css/) (root `em`) instead. Last time I checked, many people considered `em` in CSS to be a design flaw, which is why most people use `rem` in CSS nowadays. There are still a few legitimate reasons to use `em` in CSS in 2025, but `rem` is more suited in most cases.\r\n\r\nThat said, maybe it's not a relevant distinction here.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3514451023/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3514650174","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112617#issuecomment-3514650174","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112617","id":3514650174,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RfU4-","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-11T01:55:50Z","updated_at":"2025-11-11T01:55:50Z","body":"If I'm understanding `rem` correctly, it sounds like it wouldn't respect `[font_size]` BBCode blocks. That is to say, if you had the text\r\n```\r\nI said, [font_size=50]DO YOU HAVE ANY [img height=100rem]coin.png[/img] COINS??[/font_size]\r\n```\r\nand the theme/default font size for this RichTextLabel is 16px, then the `coin.png` sprite would be 16px tall, even though it's in a block of text that's 50px tall.\r\n\r\nI suppose we could include *both* `rem` and `em`; the latter would respect `[font_size]` whereas the former wouldn't. I don't know how many use cases there would be for that, though.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3514650174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3520106886","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112617#issuecomment-3520106886","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112617","id":3520106886,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7R0JGG","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-12T05:37:58Z","updated_at":"2025-11-12T05:37:58Z","body":"The `1em` measurement is equal to 100% of the surrounding font size, rather than `100em`.\r\n\r\nThis required changing the width and height values from ints to floats, so now for free the pixel sizes and percentages also support float values!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3520106886/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4207749264","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112617#issuecomment-4207749264","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112617","id":4207749264,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc76zSiQ","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-08T16:16:39Z","updated_at":"2026-04-08T16:16:39Z","body":"Thanks for the review and approval!\r\n\r\nI can see the concern with using `em` as the unit name. It may lead users to assume that other CSS units and techniques are possible with BBCode when they actually aren't.\r\n\r\nPersonally, I'd love to use `%` as that would feel the most intuitive to me, but according to the docs, `%` is used for defining a percentage of the *control width* already. I don't know what the use case would be for having a font's height be a percentage of the whole control's width, but technically that would induce a compatibility break. \r\n\r\nI'm not opposed to `fs` myself, as long as it's not an existing abbreviation for some other unit that could confuse users (which does not seem to be the case from a quick Google search). That being said, [`em` appears to be a unit outside of just CSS](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Em_(typography)), and with it already having a known definition, it may be a bit easier/more intuitive for users.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4207749264/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4224912035","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112617#issuecomment-4224912035","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112617","id":4224912035,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc770wqj","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-10T15:38:52Z","updated_at":"2026-04-10T15:38:52Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4224912035/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]